{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"no sql database no sql database","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md","fileName":"NoSQL Database.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"NoSQL Database","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-08 22:09\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Azure Cosmos DB Applications]] [[Cloud Data Storage Selection and Consistency]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Azure Cosmos DB Applications","Cloud Data Storage Selection and Consistency","Document Database","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"no sql database no sql database","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md","fileName":"NoSQL Database.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"NoSQL Database","heading":"NoSQL Database","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A NoSQL database uses a data model other than the traditional relational table-and-join model. The category includes document, key-value, graph, and other stores whose structures and scaling choices fit different access patterns.\n\nCosmos DB supplies a [[Document Database]] in the project, while its API compatibility lets the application use MongoDB conventions. Choosing NoSQL is therefore not merely choosing the cloud; it is choosing storage and query semantics that should match the application's data relationships.\n\nNoSQL stores can favor distributed writes, flexible records, and partitioned scale by relaxing relational constraints or offering weaker consistency choices. The benefit is workload-dependent rather than a universal replacement for relational data.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Azure Cosmos DB Applications","Cloud Data Storage Selection and Consistency","Document Database","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"no sql database no sql database","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/NoSQL Database.md","fileName":"NoSQL Database.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"NoSQL Database","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf]]\n[[hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Azure Cosmos DB Applications","Cloud Data Storage Selection and Consistency","Document Database","c8andnetcore30projectsusingazure.pdf","hands-onsoftwarearchitecturewithc8andnetcore3.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}